%N A398997 The binomial matrix of the number of involutions (A000085). Square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A398997 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A398997 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A398997 A(n, n) = I(n), the number of involutions.
%F A398997 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * I(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
